DwarfSpec Test Runner UI Proposal
=================================

Purpose:
    ☐ Design a Cypress-like viewer for running, observing, and triaging DwarfSpec tests.
    ☐ Optimize the primary workflow for: select scope -> run -> select test -> inspect attempt and step -> inspect evidence -> rerun or open source.
    ☐ Keep source editing, general breakpoints, variables, watches, and call-stack debugging in VS Code.
    ☐ Do not imply runtime capabilities, such as host-screen capture or replay, until their feasibility and data contracts are confirmed.

Completion contract:
    ☐ Complete every applicable component, mockup-state, prototype, organization, and audit item below.
    ☐ Treat this checklist as the source of truth for the UI proposal.
    ☐ Record every rejected or deferred item with its rationale and blocking product or runtime dependency.
    ☐ Reuse every applicable existing DFHack widget component before creating a new component or subtype.
    ☐ Document and reuse the official DFHack gui.widgets library before creating equivalent custom controls.
    ☐ Keep generic DFHack components free of DwarfSpec-specific semantics.
    ☐ Keep every complex component specimen and its variants on a dedicated, clearly named Penpot page.
    ☐ Verify component instances and dependent mockups after every master-component change.

Phase 1: Establish contracts and the DFHack widget foundation
    ☐ Exit with the product contracts, runtime capability decisions, official widget inventory, and reuse rules settled before custom component work begins.

1.1 Official DFHack gui.widgets coverage:
    ☐ Use the stable DFHack In-game UI Library documentation as the source of truth:
        - https://docs.dfhack.org/en/stable/docs/dev/Lua%20API.html#in-game-ui-library
    ☐ Maintain a Penpot coverage matrix for all 28 documented gui.widgets classes.
    ☐ Mark each widget as documented, component-linked, variant-complete, and demonstrated in a composition.
    ☐ Document Widget as the non-visual base contract for frame, frame inset, background, visibility, enabled state, focus, and parent-child layout.
    ☐ Do not create a standalone visual component for the abstract Widget base class.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing Window mockup.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing EditField variants.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing Scrollbar component.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing Label examples.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing HotkeyLabel variants.
    ☐ Verify and explicitly annotate the existing TextButton variants.
    ☐ Verify that List Box and List Item variants accurately represent widgets.List.
    ☐ Rename or annotate List Box and List Item coverage so the widgets.List relationship is explicit.

1.2 Official DFHack container and layout widget mockups:
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.Panel component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate unframed and framed Panel presentations.
        ☐ Demonstrate applicable FRAME_WINDOW, FRAME_PANEL, FRAME_MEDIUM, FRAME_THIN, FRAME_BOLD, FRAME_INTERIOR, and FRAME_INTERIOR_MEDIUM styles.
        ☐ Demonstrate title, draggable, resizable, and auto-arranged child configurations without combining unrelated states into one variant matrix.
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.ResizingPanel component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate automatic height and automatic width behavior with changing child content.
        ☐ Compose the specimen from a component-linked Panel rather than redrawing its frame.
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.Pages component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate exactly one visible child page.
        ☐ Demonstrate page selection independently from the control that triggers selection.
        ☐ Pair Pages with TabBar in a separate composition example.
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.Divider component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate horizontal and vertical dividers.
        ☐ Demonstrate straight ends, exterior T-junctions, interior T-junctions, and crossing dividers.
        ☐ Use Divider components instead of one-off rectangle lines in later component mockups.

1.3 Official DFHack text and tooltip widget mockups:
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.TextArea component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate multiline content, cursor, selection, wrapping, and scrolling.
        ☐ Demonstrate normal, focused, disabled, and read-only presentation only where supported by the widget contract.
        ☐ Compose the normal Scrollbar where scrolling is visible.
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.WrappedLabel component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate responsive wrapping at multiple widths.
        ☐ Demonstrate preserved newlines and indentation.
        ☐ Compose Label styling instead of duplicating it.
    ☐ Create a dedicated widgets.TooltipLabel component page.
        ☐ Demonstrate hidden and visible tooltip states.
        ☐ Demonstrate wrapped and non-wrapped tooltip content.
        ☐ Demonstrate TooltipLabel inside an appropriate framed Panel or Window composition.

